l involved are in different universes. The reason you can't print a newspaper cheaply isn't because Epson and HP are ripping you off (though they are, on ink), but because you're using a completely different, inherently more expensive technology that's optimized for convenience, short runs, and photo-quality output, not for cost-per-page on commodity newsprint. The two worlds of "ink on paper" have almost nothing in common beyond the final visual result.
